{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"MEASURED ON BEDROCK: caching WORKS, so this bug is specific to the direct-Anthropic path.\n\nRaw boto3 converse with a 29,400-char repeated prefix + cachePoint, us-east-1:\n  us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6  call-1 cacheWrite=6604   call-2/3 cacheRead=6604\n  us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8    call-1 cacheWrite=11404  call-2/3 cacheRead=11404\nEnd-to-end through rebar's bedrock_model.py path (19-call gate run):\n  cache_read_tokens=542,723  cache_write_tokens=6,239\n\npydantic-ai's Bedrock adapter does map cacheReadInputTokens/cacheWriteInputTokens (models/bedrock.py:676-682),\nso these are real numbers, not defaults.\n\nThis reframes the bug: the cache_read=0/cache_write=0 rebar logs on claude-opus-4-8 is NOT a\nmodel-capability fact, it is a direct-Anthropic-path fact. Moving that traffic to Bedrock fixes it.\n\nCaveat: 2 of 19 calls (plan-review-coach, ticket-digest) still logged 'caching requested but had NO\neffect'. Both were small one-off calls with no prior identical prefix, so that is expected behaviour\nrather than the defect — worth encoding in the warning's floor so it stops crying wolf on them."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785496011847154001,"uuid":"c38cb1b9-0545-4fba-b84f-fb4f8b0c421d"}